This level is very similar to the previous one — we need to submit the current password to a port on localhost. The key difference is that port 30001 requires an **SSL encrypted connection** instead of a plain text one. Using `nc` like the previous level returns nothing because the server expects an encrypted handshake first. Instead we use `openssl s_client` to establish a secure SSL connection and submit the password through it.

Why `nc` doesn't work here:-
`nc` sends data as plain text with no encryption. Port 30001 is running an SSL/TLS service that expects an encrypted connection — when `nc` connects and sends plain text, the server doesn't understand it and silently drops the connection. This is why we get no output at all.

Step-by-Step Process:-

**Step 1 — Log into bandit15**
```bash
