What is a Setuid Binary?
In Linux, every file has an owner and a set of permissions. Normally, when you run a program, it runs with **your** permissions. A setuid (Set User ID) binary is different — it runs with the permissions of the **file's owner** instead.

You can spot a setuid binary by running `ls -la`:
